 ### X-Bucket and X-Actives Processing
-This variant involves processing scanlines from bottom to top. For each scanline, a 'critical section' of code is entered, where only one processor can run at a time [S6]. The surviving polygons of the previous pixel's x-actives list must be updated with newly interpolated values of field data and screen-z. New screen-z values may require rearrangement of polygons among survivors to maintain screen-z order [S6]. Taking into account the line-of-sight distance between the two polygons, the color-opacity contribution for that inter-polygon region is calculated and composited into a software floating point frame buffer using standard equations [S6].
